# Gesture control end to end. Run: emu/tests/run-gesture-test.sh (it sets KICK_EMU_GESTURES=1 and checks the app log too).
# The Surface plays the part of kick-gesture: it sends gesture events to the app's IPC server, the app maps them to panel
# input, and the bank LEDs show the swipes. Palm, fist and pinch have no LED change, so the wrapper script checks the app
# log for the buttons and knob they press.
expect connected
wait 24000

# Open the first demo project so the banks exist (bank A is selected on load).
button Enter
wait 10000
expect led Bank A on

# Swipe right selects the next bank.
gesture swipe_right
expect led Bank B on
gesture swipe_right
expect led Bank C on

# Swipe left from bank A wraps to H. Go back to A first with two swipes left from C.
gesture swipe_left
gesture swipe_left
gesture swipe_left
expect led Bank H on

# Open palm presses Play, fist presses Stop.
gesture palm_hold
wait 500
gesture fist
wait 500

# A pinch turns Q-Link knob 1: start, then the hand opens in steps.
gesture pinch_start 0.2
wait 200
gesture pinch_change 0.4
wait 200
gesture pinch_change 0.7
wait 200
gesture pinch_change 0.9
wait 500
gesture pinch_end 0.9
wait 500

# Normal panel input still works after gestures.
button Pad Mix
wait 1000
snapshot gesture-surface.png
quit
